# OverCut licensing

OverCut is open source and uses two licences, split by directory (decision: `docs/adr/0009-license.md`).

| Part | Path | Licence | Text |
|---|---|---|---|
| Apps (UI, web/PWA, desktop and mobile shells) | `apps/*` | GPL-3.0-or-later | `LICENSE-GPL` |
| Engine crates | `crates/*` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 (your choice) | `LICENSE-MIT`, `LICENSE-APACHE` |
| Shared packages (e.g. engine client) | `packages/*` | MIT OR Apache-2.0 (your choice) | `LICENSE-MIT`, `LICENSE-APACHE` |
| Docs, scripts, tests, tooling | everything else | GPL-3.0-or-later unless a file says otherwise | `LICENSE-GPL` |

The permissive engine and package code may be combined into the GPL apps; the reverse is not allowed (GPL code may not be pulled into `crates/*` or `packages/*`).

Contributions are accepted under the same licence as the part they touch, with a DCO sign-off (no CLA). See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

**No feature gating, ever**: see `docs/GOVERNANCE.md`.
